# Grounded 2025-10-10 in the user's own account of a 2025 encounter (full
# account: focus/F34/notes.md). The harder edges of that account -- an
# entity's opening move, and the difficult passage that followed -- are not
# scripted here as something to expect; a briefing is not the place to
# rehearse a fear-and-confrontation scenario for a future listener. What
# carries over is the shape of the place and the tools that helped: the
# gathering itself, the option not to engage, and the anchor.
#
# No longer @provisional -- this is one account, not a settled description,
# and says so in its own text rather than hiding behind the tag.

@segment     briefing-f34
@title       Focus 34 — The Gathering
@levels      F34
@duration    ~1m10s

say You are now in Focus 34.
pause 5
say Behind you, the Park at Focus 27. Ahead, Focus 35, and further gathering beyond.
pause 6
say This is a place of gathering. Others may be present, drawn from further than the physical universe accounts for. You may notice them, or you may not — either is a complete visit.
pause 10
say If you do notice presence, there is no requirement to engage. Approach it the way you'd want to be approached: gracefully, without demanding anything.
pause 10
say If anything here feels difficult to hold, perception tends to respond to intention more directly than it does at home. A shift in thought can be enough to change what you're perceiving.
pause 10
say If you feel unmoored, give yourself something ordinary to hold onto. Anything familiar will do. It's often enough to bring things back to steady.
pause 10
say What's written here is drawn from one visit, not a settled description. Let your own account, if you keep one, stand beside it rather than under it.
pause 10
say Stay as briefly or as long as feels right.
pause 8
